        <body>
            <div xml:id="d578">

                <pb facs="1006" n="910" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg910"/>

                <head>No. 576.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Cushing.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-08-27"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 27,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 61.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I acknowledge the receipt of your
                    interesting dispatch of the 30th ultimo, No. 66, in relation to the possibility
                    of European intervention in the affairs of Spain. It confirms accounts which
                    have reached this country of atrocities in warfare which seem incredible in the
                    nineteenth century, which are without excuse or palliation, and a continuance of
                    which would be degrading to human nature.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
